1
00:00:00,541 --> 00:00:03,083
Part 5: Feeding Tubes

2
00:00:03,375 --> 00:00:04,625
A feeding tube can be

3
00:00:04,625 --> 00:00:09,250
placed in one of two ways,
through the nose and into the stomach,

4
00:00:09,250 --> 00:00:12,750
or directly through the skin
into the stomach.

5
00:00:13,041 --> 00:00:15,250
The first tube, through the nose

6
00:00:15,250 --> 00:00:18,916
and into the stomach
is called a dobhoff tube.

7
00:00:19,166 --> 00:00:23,166
The insertion of a tube
through the nose, through the esophagus,

8
00:00:23,166 --> 00:00:27,833
and into the stomach is a procedure
that we can perform in the clinic.

9
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:31,750
It is a relatively quick procedure,
and the tube can be removed

10
00:00:31,750 --> 00:00:35,708
easily as soon as eating food
by mouth is adequate

11
00:00:35,708 --> 00:00:39,041
and your body weight has stabilized
and increased.

12
00:00:39,375 --> 00:00:42,375
This tube is typically
a temporary solution

13
00:00:42,375 --> 00:00:45,791
and can last for a few days
to a few weeks.

14
00:00:46,041 --> 00:00:49,208
Dobhoff Tubes do not require a scheduled date or 

15
00:00:49,208 --> 00:00:53,541
overnight stay due to the relative simplicity of insertion.  

16
00:00:54,916 --> 00:00:59,291
The placement of a dobhoff tube
does not need image guidance.

17
00:00:59,291 --> 00:01:05,000
However, after insertion of a dobhoff tube,
through the nose and into the stomach.

18
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:08,958
an X-ray of the chest will be taken
to confirm the proper placement

19
00:01:08,958 --> 00:01:11,916
of the end of the tube
inside the stomach.

20
00:01:12,458 --> 00:01:15,208
The second tube, directly through the skin
and into the stomach,

21
00:01:15,208 --> 00:01:16,583
The second tube, directly through the skin
and into the stomach,

22
00:01:17,416 --> 00:01:22,541
is called a Percutaneous Endogastric 
Gastrostomy Tube  or Peg tube.

23
00:01:22,541 --> 00:01:25,583
This tube is a more permanent intervention

24
00:01:25,583 --> 00:01:30,125
and is surprisingly more common
than dobhoff tubes.

25
00:01:30,125 --> 00:01:32,833
However, just because they're popular

26
00:01:32,833 --> 00:01:36,583
doesn't mean they're good. 
Compared to dobhoff tubes,

27
00:01:36,583 --> 00:01:41,500
Peg tubes pose a greater number of 
challenges with insertion and use.

28
00:01:42,583 --> 00:01:44,958
First, the insertion of a peg tube

29
00:01:44,958 --> 00:01:50,125
is somewhat more invasive than a
dobhoff tube. To be placed correctly,

30
00:01:50,125 --> 00:01:53,250
The peg tube needs to be inserted
by a specialist called an

31
00:01:53,250 --> 00:01:57,583
Interventional Radiologist,
with the assistance of image guidance.

32
00:01:58,375 --> 00:02:03,250
PEG tubes can be placed in different ways 
with varying degrees of invasiveness-

33
00:02:03,541 --> 00:02:08,333
from image guidance, to minimal surgery 
(laparoscopic), all the way to open surgery.

34
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:12,875
Open surgery is the most aggressive placement option.

35
00:02:13,625 --> 00:02:17,208
Unlike Dobhoff Tubes, due to greater invasiveness,

36
00:02:17,208 --> 00:02:20,875
PEG Tube Insertions cannot be performed in the clinic

37
00:02:20,875 --> 00:02:24,000
and require both a scheduled and overnight stay.

38
00:02:24,750 --> 00:02:30,333
Second, PEG tubes require a special 
type of food called tube feeds.

39
00:02:30,333 --> 00:02:34,166
Tube feeds are a different
 composition from regular food.

40
00:02:34,166 --> 00:02:37,583
Because of this,
your body will have to learn how to digest

41
00:02:37,583 --> 00:02:41,041
this new food source
and may take several days.

42
00:02:41,708 --> 00:02:45,833
Third, in addition to your body
learning this new food source,

43
00:02:45,833 --> 00:02:49,500
you will also have to learn how,
when and where

44
00:02:49,500 --> 00:02:51,875
to have tube feeds ordered and delivered.

45
00:02:52,291 --> 00:02:55,541
Our dietitian will assist you
with this task.
